  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 2(4) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, a person is defined as 'counterfeiting' if they cause one thing to resemble another with the intention of practicing deception or with knowledge that such resemblance is likely to deceive others. Furthermore, Section 2(4) Explanation 2 establishes a presumption of intent to deceive when a resemblance is likely to mislead a person. An illustration in Section 318(1) demonstrates this by showing a scenario where a person puts a counterfeit mark on an article to deceive another into believing it is from a celebrated manufacturer, thereby inducing them to purchase it.",
